n why Norwich uses a bugler, rather than recorded field music, for daily calls.","short_summary":"Norwich’s daily Reveille practice retains live bugle calls rather than recorded field music.","evidence_claim":"The Norwich Cadet Handbook says it has always been Norwich custom for a bugler to sound all bugle calls and that recorded field music has not been used for these daily ceremonies.","source_url":"https://home.norwich.edu/documents/cadet-handbook","source_title":"Norwich University Cadet Handbook","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Observe only from authorized public or campus-accessible areas and follow event staff directions.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"norwich-retreat","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Retreat","title":"Observe Retreat at Day’s End","subtitle":"Daily national-colors ceremony","notes":"Consult the Cadet Handbook for the day-end flag ceremony and its sequence of bugle call, honors, and lowering of the Colors.","short_summary":"A daily ceremony marking the lowering of the national flag at the end of the day.","evidence_claim":"The Norwich Cadet Handbook describes Reveille and Retreat as daily ceremonies honoring the national flag at its raising and lowering, respectively.","source_url":"https://home.norwich.edu/documents/cadet-handbook","source_title":"Norwich University Cadet Handbook","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Observe only from authorized public or campus-accessible areas and follow event staff directions.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"norwich-i-will-try-motto","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"“I Will Try” Motto","title":"Trace the “I Will Try” Tradition","subtitle":"Norwich’s enduring university motto","notes":"Visit the Sullivan Museum’s interpretation of the 1844 flag and the competing stories surrounding the motto’s deeper history.","short_summary":"A campus motto with an early material record and a carefully documented origin story.","evidence_claim":"Norwich’s Sullivan Museum says an 1844 flag demonstrates that “I’ll Try” was in use at least three years before the often-repeated Ransom-at-Chapultepec story.","source_url":"https://www.norwich.edu/campus-resources/library-archives-museum/sullivan-museum-and-history-center/exhibitions","source_title":"Sullivan Museum and History Center Exhibitions","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The museum’s exhibit page documents the flag and explains that the motto’s origin story has competing interpretations.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
